## Optional Dependencies (Enabled via Environment Variables / CLI Flags)

### litellm
- License: MIT
- URL: https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm
- Used for: Unified LLM API (100+ providers), enabled by LLM_MODEL env var
- Note: Optional; DeepSeek direct connection remains the default

### py-fsrs
- License: MIT
- URL: https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition/py-fsrs
- Used for: Spaced repetition scheduling in `plan --fsrs`
- Note: Optional; falls back to 1/2/4/7/15/30 day progression

### pkuseg
- License: MIT
- URL: https://github.com/lancopku/pkuseg-python
- Used for: Medical-domain Chinese word segmentation, enabled by USE_PKUSEG=1
- Note: Optional; jieba remains the default

### markmap
- License: MIT
- URL: https://github.com/markmap/markmap
- Used for: Interactive HTML mindmap export (mindmap.html)
- Note: Loaded via jsDelivr CDN at runtime; no build step required

### PaddleOCR
- License: Apache 2.0
- URL: https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR
- Used for: OCR of scanned PDFs and image-based exam papers (USE_OCR=1)
- Note: Optional; pdfplumber remains the default for text-layer PDFs

### PyMuPDF (fitz)
- License: AGPL-3.0 / commercial dual license
- URL: https://github.com/pymupdf/pymupdf
- Used for: Rendering scanned PDF pages to images for OCR fallback
- Note: Used only at runtime inside the OCR fallback path; if you distribute
  a modified binary including this path, AGPL obligations may apply.
  For a fully MIT-only pipeline, use text-layer PDFs only.

### genanki
- License: MIT
- URL: https://github.com/kerrickstaley/genanki
- Used for: Exporting wrong-question book to Anki .apkg decks
- Note: Optional; `wrong export --format anki`

### openpyxl
- License: MIT
- URL: https://github.com/openpyxl/openpyxl
- Used for: Exporting wrong-question book to Excel .xlsx
- Note: Optional; `wrong export --format excel`

### rank_bm25
- License: Apache 2.0
- URL: https://github.com/dorianbrown/rank_bm25
- Used for: Local offline similar-question retrieval (BM25 algorithm)
- Note: Optional; `similar` command

